  "name": "Ossetian song and Nart kadaeg (North Ossetia)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Song tradition of the Ossetians, an Iranian-speaking people of the central Caucasus centred on Vladikavkaz. Men's songs set a solo voice against a male chorus that holds a lower supporting part, and the heroic kadaeg, including songs of the Nart sagas, were traditionally sung to the bowed kissyn-fandyr; the accordion accompanies song and dance, as does the plucked dala-fandyr, which this default leaves out. The repertoire is documented on Melodiya Ossetian folk LPs.",
  "recipe": "classic modern ossetian song and nart kadaeg, drone Modal, vocal branch. solo over vocal choral drone. melodic bowed song accompaniment kissyn fandyr, reedy mountain toned garmon. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
